  "overview": "From 2026-02-08 to 2026-02-15, ethereum-optimism/op-geth had 1 new PRs (0 merged), 1 new issues, and 35 active contributors.",
  "topIssues": [
    {
      "id": "I_kwDOH2Qg5s7pW9k7",
      "title": "Support multiple sequencer RPC endpoints for transaction forwarding",
      "author": "brendontan03",
      "number": 763,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/op-geth",
      "body": "## Summary\nSupport configuring multiple sequencer RPC endpoints for op-geth with automatic failover when one endpoint is unavailable. Currently, --rollup.sequencerhttp only accepts a single URL; if that endpoint fails (e.g. CDN or regional outage), all transaction submission to the sequencer fails.\n\n## Rationale\n- Operators and third-party RPCs can only set one rollup.sequencer-http endpoint.\n- A single point of failure: if that RPC is down or unreachable, eth_sendRawTransaction (and any other sequencer-forwarded calls) will fail for all users.\n- There is no way to configure redundant official RPCs for higher availability.\n\n## Implementation\n- Allow multiple sequencer RPC URLs via a comma-separated value\n- Keep backward compatibility where a single URL continues to work\n\n### Failover behaviour\n- When forwarding a transaction (or other sequencer RPC call) to the current endpoint fails, automatically try the next configured endpoint.\n- Continue until one succeeds or all fail; then return the last error to the caller.\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-02-09T08:28:17Z",
      "closedAt": null,
      "state": "OPEN",
      "commentCount": 4
    }
  ],
  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOH2Qg5s7DN0uz",
      "title": "feat: support multi sequencer http",
      "author": "brendontan03",
      "number": 764,
      "body": "**Description**\r\n\r\nSupport multiple sequencer RPC endpoints for op-geth with automatic failover when one endpoint is unavailable.\r\n\r\n#### Implementation\r\n- `--rollup.sequencerhttp` now accepts comma-separated URLs for redundancy\r\n- Add additional flags `--rollup.sequencer-dial-timeout` and `--rollup.sequencer-request-timeout` to control request and dialing timeouts\r\n- Automatic failover on connection/transport errors (5xx, timeouts, connection refused, etc.)\r\n- Application errors (e.g. \"nonce too low\") will not trigger failover\r\n\r\n**Tests**\r\n\r\n- Add unit tests to verify functionality /rpc/sequencerclient_test.go\r\n- Run using this command `go test -v -run Sequencer ./rpc/`\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n\r\nFailover Logic:\r\n- Maintains a preferredIndex which represents the index of the currently active endpoint\r\n- On failure, cycles through remaining endpoints: if on endpoint 3, tries 4, 5, ..., N, then 1, 2\r\n- Each endpoint is tried exactly once per request before failing\r\n- On successful RPC call, that endpoint's index becomes the new preferredIndex\r\n- Connections are cached and reused until they fail\r\n\r\n**Metadata**\r\n\r\n- Fixes https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/op-geth/issues/763\r\n\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/op-geth",
      "createdAt": "2026-02-12T09:00:57Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 766,
      "deletions": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOH2Qg5s6nd40T",
      "title": "core: Log DA usage estimates",
      "author": "sebastianst",
